1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,550
Changes-in-changes — The whole counterfactual distribution, not just the mean

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:08,950
DiD compares averages. Changes-in-changes (Athey & Imbens 2006) recovers the whole counterfactual distribution.

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,950
In the control group, see how each rank of the distribution moved over time: the 10th, 50th and 90th percentiles.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,450
Give each treated unit the change that a control unit with the same before-period outcome experienced.

5
00:00:23,500 --> 00:00:30,950
Compare the actual treated distribution with this counterfactual: there is an effect at every quantile, larger at the top.

6
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:38,950
Unlike DiD, the answer does not depend on whether the outcome is measured in levels or logs. Stata: cic.
